### Downstream Breaking Changes

<a id="finding-pr-43745-sdk-enum-shape"></a>
### Generated SKU enum shape and member identity change

- **Severity:** high
- **Confidence:** high
- **Summary:** The wire contract remains compatible, but generated clients can replace a fixed enum with an extensible string-backed shape and rename the second source member from an identity containing `Standard B10` to `StandardB10`; construction, comparison, exhaustive handling, and references to the prior member can break.
- **Evidence:** The only AutoRest schema difference changes x-ms-enum modelAsString from false to true and preserves wire values Standard_B1 and Standard B10.; Generated clients change from a fixed enum to an extensible string-backed shape.; The generated member name for the wire value Standard B10 changes to StandardB10 while the serialized value remains Standard B10.
- **TypeSpec source:** [models.tsp:L286-L293](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/71ce7d0c524c4bea7bc737836684acd53f343147/specification/hardwaresecuritymodules/resource-manager/Microsoft.HardwareSecurityModules/HardwareSecurityModules/models.tsp#L286-L293)


